### star-plan-executor/SKILL.md
--- 1
**Hand Step 5 to the EXEC tier.** With EXEC_PLAN, EXEC_LOG, and all currently required decisions recorded, dispatch one `Agent` subagent (`subagent_type: star-exec`, `model:` the EXEC value) when that entry names a model that is not an alias of this run's (conventions §10.8) or a depth this run is not already on, and this run is not already `tier=exec`. It reads this manifest and resumes from Step 5 with `involve=<level> tier=exec` and any valid `auto=unattended` grant. It may not edit EXEC_PLAN or improvise around a plan-level gap. A STOP-line command or unresolved blocked-edit decision is recorded and returned to the user-facing run; an existing applicable decision is reused. Wait for the delegate to finish â its completion, not an interim reply â then re-read EXEC_LOG and continue at Step 6; never begin verification while it may still be writing that log. With no usable model override or `Agent` route, run Step 5 here without asking repeatedly for unavailable machinery.
+++ 1
**Hand Step 5 to the EXEC tier.** With records and decisions settled, when the EXEC entry names a model that is not an alias of this run's (conventions §10.8) or a depth this run is not already on, and this run is not already `tier=exec`, dispatch `Agent` (`subagent_type: coder`; pass the EXEC model, or the pool alias binding its configured depth, when the configured pool supports it — a configured depth is reason enough to dispatch even when the model aliases this session's) to read this manifest and resume from Step 5 with `involve=<level> tier=exec` and any valid `auto=unattended` grant. It may not edit EXEC_PLAN or improvise around a plan-level gap. Wait for the delegate to finish â its completion, not an interim reply â then re-read EXEC_LOG, never verifying while it may still be writing that log; with no such override, or if unavailable, run Step 5 here.
